    "title": "What channel is Arkansas basketball vs Ole Miss on today? Time, TV schedule, prediction",
    "text": "Updated March 14, 2026, 7:24 a.m. CTNASHVILLE, Tenn. — Arkansas basketball will have to derail a Cinderella on an improbable run if it wants to reach the SEC Tournament Championship.The Razorbacks (24-8) will face No. 15 Ole Miss in the semifinals on Saturday, March 14. The Rebels (15-19) finished tied for last in the league standings, but they are now two wins away from securing an automatic berth into the NCAA Tournament.Arkansas opened its postseason with an 82-79 win over Oklahoma in the quarterfinals on Friday. Darius Acuff Jr. scored 37 points and Arkansas got second-half contributions from the entire roster in a narrow in.Ole Miss has won three games in three days, starting with a victory over Texas before pulling stunning upsets over Georgia and Alabama. The Rebels would be the first Power 4 team with a losing record to make the NCAA Tournament if they finish off this magical run.Here's a look at how to watch today's SEC Semifinal between Arkansas and Ole Miss.Stream Arkansas basketball vs Ole Miss in SEC TournamentWhat channel is Arkansas basketball vs Ole Miss on today?TV Channel: ESPNLivestream: Fubo (free trial), ESPN+Arkansas vs. Ole Miss will broadcast nationally on ESPN. Karl Ravech and Jimmy Dykes will call the game from Bridgestone Arena, with Alyssa Lang reporting from the sidelines. The game is available to stream on Fubo, which offers a free trial to new subscribers, and ESPN+.Arkansas basketball vs Ole Miss time todayDate: Saturday, March 14Start time: 2:30 p.m. CTThe Arkansas vs. Ole Miss game is scheduled to start at 2:30 p.m., or 25 minutes after the conclusion of the preceding game.Stream Arkansas vs Ole MissArkansas basketball vs Ole Miss predictionOle Miss is playing its best basketball of the season, but the Rebels will finally run out of gas in their fourth game in as many days. Look for Meleek Thomas to have a strong game and Darius Acuff Jr. to continue his torrid close to the year. Arkansas 90, Ole Miss 83.Arkansas basketball’s potential SEC Tournament scheduleFriday, March 13: Arkansas 82, Oklahoma 79.Saturday, March 14: Semifinals vs. Ole MissSunday, March 15: Final vs. Florida or VanderbiltJackson Fuller covers Arkansas football, basketball and baseball for the Southwest Times Record, part of the USA TODAY Network. Reach him at jfuller@usatodayco.com or follow him@jacksonfuller16 on X, formerly known as Twitter. Our team of savvy editors independently handpicks all recommendations. If you purchase through our links, the USA TODAY Network may earn a commission. Prices were accurate at the time of publication but may change.",
